schema: "0.4"
id: npl-nocturne-36-agent-memory-browser
type: image
quality: high

# NoizuPromptLingo (a prompt-definition language + MCP toolchain for agent engineers) — Agent Memory Browser screen.
# Theme tenets: dark-native near-black canvas, single phosphor-green "live" signal, mono-first, 4px radius, flat surface-step elevation (no glow/gradient).
# Palette: canvas #010409, panel #0d1117, raised #161b22, text #e6edf3, secondary #909dab, signal green #3fb950, link cyan #58a6ff, amber #d29922.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    dark-native agent-engineering instrument — a dense, multi-panel monitor you
    watch during long sessions. Cool terminal dark throughout; the ONLY saturated
    color is a single phosphor-green "live" signal, with a rare amber caution.
    Monospace is a co-equal voice (IDs, timestamps, scores render mono). Flat
    surfaces separated by lightness steps, never drop shadows or glow.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of the Agent Memory Browser screen of
    NoizuPromptLingo — a read-only inspector for a persona's memory store.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (three panels on a 1440-class viewport, visible together
    without scrolling): a slim LEFT NAV RAIL on the darkest near-black canvas, a
    LEFT FILTER column, and a dominant CENTER results stream — all on lighter dark
    panel tones stepped by lightness.

    TOP SEARCH BAND: a wide SEMANTIC RECALL SEARCH BAR (a recessed input cut one
    step darker than its panel, mono placeholder "semantic recall…", a small search
    glyph), and to its right a compact RECALL LATENCY METER — a small readout card
    showing a mono millisecond value and a tiny sparkline, labeled "recall latency".

    LEFT FILTER PANEL — EMOTIONAL VALENCE FILTER: a titled panel with a vertical
    list of valence facets (e.g. "positive", "neutral", "negative", "signature"),
    small selectable rows, one active with a quiet green outline; a compact legend.

    CENTER RESULTS STREAM: a dense vertical list of MEMORY ROWS. Each row: a mono
    similarity SCORE (e.g. "0.94") at the left, a one-line memory snippet in
    off-white, a small MEMORY WEIGHT INDICATOR (a short horizontal bar or dot scale
    showing reinforcement weighting), and a mono timestamp. One row carries an
    amber QUARANTINE STATUS BADGE ("quarantined") and is visibly dimmed/held out of
    normal results. A couple of rows show a lit phosphor-green "reinforced" marker.
    Rows separated by quiet dark hairlines, comfortable density.

    PALETTE & TYPE: cool near-black canvas, lighter dark panels, soft off-white
    text, cool grey secondary; phosphor-green reserved for the active filter, the
    reinforced markers; amber used once, for the quarantine caution. Inter for UI;
    JetBrains Mono for scores, timestamps, and the latency readout — mono prominent.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: 4px radius on cards and inputs, 2px on the small badge; flat
    fills, elevation by surface-lightness steps; the search input recessed. No
    gradients, no glow, no scanlines.

    MOOD: focused, instrument-like, watching a lot of signal at once — quiet chrome,
    green means live, amber means hold.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, neon glow, bloom, CRT scanlines, gradient background, pure-black OLED background, pure-white surfaces"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches Agent Memory Browser: semantic recall search bar, emotional valence filter panel, a results stream of memory rows with similarity scores + weight indicators, a quarantine badge, and a recall latency meter"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Dark-native multi-panel density, single phosphor-green signal, one rare amber caution, mono scores/timestamps, 4px radius, flat surface-step elevation, no glow/gradient"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Three-panel instrument layout visible together, clear hierarchy, dense but legible"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "neon glow, bloom, or gradient wash (breaks the flat dark instrument register)"

tags: [npl-nocturne, NoizuPromptLingo, screen-mockup]
